   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia is supporting improved governance in Bougainville&#x2019;s law and justice sector through technical assistance to the Bougainville Law and Justice Coordinating Mechanism. This includes support to implement the 2023&#x2013;26 Strategic Development Plan, develop a Memorandum of Understanding between Community Courts and Auxiliary Police, and establish a Communications Sub-Committee. Australia  also supported the rollout of whistleblower legislation and improved employment conditions for justice officials. These efforts are enhancing accountability, transparency, and coordination across Bougainville&#x2019;s Law and Justice sector. Once example being the development and implementation of the Bougainville Community Courts Bill in community courts across the region.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Disability equity</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2024, Australia supported two organisations for persons with disabilities to commence the process to establish Provincial Coordinating Committees on Disability in Morobe and West New Britain. These committees will promote inclusive decision-making and improve access to justice, particularly for women and children with disabilities. Support included technical advice, logistics, and capacity building in planning, implementation and reporting.  The committees have commenced planning on a revised composition for each committee structure and advocacy and awareness plans for their respective provinces. Australia will expand this initiative to four additional provinces under the PNG&#x2013;Australia Law and Justice Partnership.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender equality</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the Community Justice Fund, Australia supports the Salvation Army&#x2019;s House of Hope to provide safe accommodation and rehabilitation for women affected by gender-based violence. In 2024, the House of Hope supported the recovery and safe repatriation of many survivors.    This included a young survivor of sexual abuse and trafficking, who through the program received emergency shelter, medical care, and life skills training. She was safely returned to her home province and is now rebuilding her life with dignity and support.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
